#
# Counter-example for gmeow:TeachingShape: the teacher and the learner are the
# SAME agent (ex:alice). gmeow:TeachingShape's sh:sparql constraint forbids
# teacher = learner ("an agent cannot teach itself"), so validation MUST emit
# shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent (and no other finding — teacher/learner minCount,
# maxCount, and sh:class gmeow:Agent are all satisfied, subjectTaught is present).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecTeachingSelf). Lives under tests/
# (NOT examples/) so the global make validate gate does not reject it.
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/lrn/> .

ex:alice a gmeow:Agent .
ex:welding a gmeow:Skill .

ex:bad a gmeow:Teaching ;
    gmeow:teacher ex:alice ;
    gmeow:learner ex:alice ;
    gmeow:subjectTaught ex:welding .
